{"ts": "2026-11-06T23:28:00Z", "by": "model:gemini", "entity": "specimen", "id": "C340", "op": "set", "field": "story", "old": "A Japanese 100 yen coin dated Heisei 27 (2015). One side is filled with cherry blossoms, the sakura, Japan's beloved unofficial national flower; the other carries a big, plain 100. This design has served on the 100 yen since 1967, across three emperors.", "new": "A Japanese 100 yen coin dated Heisei 27 (2015). One side is filled with cherry blossoms, the sakura, Japan's beloved unofficial national flower; the other carries a big, plain 100. This design has served on the 100 yen since 1967, across three emperors.", "source": "https://en.numista.com/catalogue/pieces2121.html (\"Emperor: Heisei (1989-2019) | Obverse: Cherry blossoms, authority above, value below (日本国 百円) | Reverse: Large value in center, date below | Edge: Reeded\")", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "high", "provenance": {"model": "gemini", "prompt_version": "HOMEWORK@2026-11-05", "workflow": "homework-story-check", "assignment": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261105-1", "run_id": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261105-1", "inputs": [{"file": "https://en.numista.com/catalogue/pieces2121.html"}], "raw": "compact answer S3"}}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T23:28:00Z", "by": "model:gemini", "entity": "specimen", "id": "C341", "op": "set", "field": "story", "old": "An East German 10 pfennig from 1968, feather-light aluminium. One side carries the state emblem, a hammer and compass inside a wreath of wheat, ringed by the words Deutsche Demokratische Republik; the other has a big 10 over an oak leaf. Coins like this were the small change of the DDR until the state itself vanished in 1990.", "new": "An East German 10 pfennig from 1968, feather-light aluminium. One side carries the state emblem, a hammer and compass inside a wreath of wheat, ringed by the words Deutsche Demokratische Republik; the other has a big 10 over an oak leaf. Coins like this were the small change of the DDR until the state itself vanished in 1990.", "source": "https://en.numista.com/catalogue/pieces1925.html (\"Composition: Aluminium | Weight: 1.5 g | Obverse: State emblem (hammer and a compass, surrounded by a ring of rye...) | Reverse: The value and an oak leaf and the mintmark above\")", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "high", "provenance": {"model": "gemini", "prompt_version": "HOMEWORK@2026-11-05", "workflow": "homework-story-check", "assignment": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261105-1", "run_id": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261105-1", "inputs": [{"file": "https://en.numista.com/catalogue/pieces1925.html"}], "raw": "compact answer S4"}}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T23:28:00Z", "by": "model:gemini", "entity": "specimen", "id": "C342", "op": "set", "field": "story", "old": "A South Korean 10 won from 2001, struck in brass. The Dabotap pagoda of Bulguksa temple stands on one side, a stone pagoda from the 700s and one of Korea's national treasures, with the value in Hangul beside it. The other side carries a big 10, the year, and the Bank of Korea's name. This brass design ran from 1983 to 2006, when a smaller, cheaper copper-colored version took its place; the collection already holds that successor.", "new": "A South Korean 10 won from 2001, struck in brass. The Dabotap pagoda of Bulguksa temple stands on one side, a stone pagoda from the 700s and one of Korea's national treasures, with the value in Hangul beside it. The other side carries a big 10, the year, and the Bank of Korea's name. This brass design ran from 1983 to 2006, when a smaller, cheaper copper-colored version took its place; the collection already holds that successor.", "source": "https://en.numista.com/catalogue/pieces978.html (\"Composition: Brass (65% Copper, 35% Zinc) | Weight: 4.06 g | Obverse: Dabotap Pagoda, located in Gyeongju, it is one of the national treasures dividing the value in Hangul\")", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "high", "provenance": {"model": "gemini", "prompt_version": "HOMEWORK@2026-11-05", "workflow": "homework-story-check", "assignment": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261105-1", "run_id": "HW-gemini-story-check-20261105-1", "inputs": [{"file": "https://en.numista.com/catalogue/pieces978.html"}], "raw": "compact answer S5"}}
